  "id": "sampling-error",
  "term": "sampling error",
  "definition": "Sampling error is the uncertainty that occurs because values are estimated from sample data rather than measured exactly for every member of a population. In this context, it means that survey-based estimates can vary by chance, which can make scores or rankings less stable.",
