      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly state the core statistical definition that sampling error arises because population values are “estimated from sample data rather than measured exactly for every member of a population.” It only discusses uncertainty from sampling error in ACS data in the context of a social vulnerability index.",
        "While the packet supports the general idea that survey-derived estimates/indices show “instability” (e.g., uncertainty-aware composite estimates, categorical ranking shifts, and theme stability/uncertainty), it does not clearly support the specific phrasing that survey-based estimates “vary by chance” as stated in the definition."
